Question 6) "After stealing the credentials from the config file, the attacker authenticates to the MySQL service on the victim. Using the Wireshark filter mysql.login_request, what is the timestamp (UTC) of the attacker's first MySQL login attempt?"
-------------

After filtering for "mysql.login_request". We are met with a series of login attempts. 

The login attempts shown are only attacker side requests, we cannot yet see the server responses. Because of this, I noted the frame numbers and found their corresponding responses in the TCP stream. 

There were some attempts around 11:47AM, but these were fruitless, and no subsequent application data traffic was seen after this. Additionally, I had a screenshot of the config.php compromise, and the timestamp was later than this.
Therefore at the time of these attempts, the attacker did not have credentials yet. 

Thus, the next attempts at 12:08 and 12:16 were made with the stolen credentials. The first of which being 12:08PM.

